# 基础词 Unit02
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-基础词
# 描述: 基础词Unit02核心词汇

{{adjust}}{/əˈdʒʌst/}{{v. 调整；适应}}{{Please adjust the volume to a comfortable level.}}
{{administration}}{/ədˌmɪnɪˈstreɪʃn/}{{n. 管理；行政}}{{The school administration decided to extend the假期.}}
{{admire}}{/ədˈmaɪər/}{{v. 钦佩；欣赏}}{{I admire her courage and determination.}}
{{admit}}{/ədˈmɪt/}{{v. 承认；准许进入}}{{He admitted that he had made a mistake.}}
{{adopt}}{/əˈdɒpt/}{{v. 采纳；收养}}{{The company adopted a new marketing strategy.}}
{{adult}}{/əˈdʌlt/{{n. 成年人；adj. 成年的}}{{This movie is suitable for adult audiences.}}
{{advance}}{/ədˈvɑːns/}{{v. 前进；推进；n. 进步}}{{Technology continues to advance at a rapid pace.}}
{{advantage}}{/ədˈvɑːntɪdʒ/}{{n. 优势；有利条件}}{{Being bilingual is a great advantage in today's job market.}}
{{adventure}}{/ədˈventʃər/}{{n. 冒险；奇遇}}{{They went on an adventure in the Amazon rainforest.}}
{{advertise}}{/ˈædvərtaɪz/}{{v. 做广告；宣传}}{{The company advertises its products on television.}}
{{advice}}{/ədˈvaɪs/}{{n. 建议；忠告}}{{She gave me some useful advice on studying.}}
{{advise}}{/ədˈvaɪz/}{{v. 建议；忠告}}{{The doctor advised him to quit smoking.}}
{{advocate}}{/ˈædvəkeɪt/}{{v. 提倡；n. 倡导者}}{{She advocates for equal rights for all citizens.}}
{{affair}}{/əˈfeər/}{{n. 事务；事件}}{{The government handles foreign affairs carefully.}}
{{affect}}{/əˈfekt/}{{v. 影响；感动}}{{The weather can affect our mood significantly.}}
{{afford}}{/əˈfɔːrd/}{{v. 负担得起；提供}}{{I cannot afford to buy a new car right now.}}
{{afraid}}{/əˈfreɪd/}{{adj. 害怕的；恐惧的}}{{She is afraid of speaking in public.}}
{{after}}{/ˈɑːftər/}{{prep./conj. 在…之后}}{{We went for a walk after dinner.}}
{{again}}{/əˈɡen/}{{adv. 再一次；又}}{{Could you please say that again?}}
{{against}}{/əˈɡenst/}{{prep. 反对；靠着}}{{He leaned against the wall and休息.}}
{{age}}{/eɪdʒ/}{{n. 年龄；时代}}{{Children of all ages enjoy this game.}}
{{agency}}{/ˈeɪdʒənsi/}{{n. 代理机构；部门}}{{She works for a travel agency downtown.}}
{{agenda}}{/əˈdʒendə/}{{n. 议程；日程}}{{The agenda for today's meeting is very long.}}
{{agent}}{/ˈeɪdʒənt/}{{n. 代理人；特工}}{{He works as a real estate agent.}}
{{aggressive}}{/əˈɡresɪv/}{{adj. 侵略性的；有进取心的}}{{The company has an aggressive expansion plan.}}
{{ago}}{/əˈɡəʊ/}{{adv. 以前}}{{I graduated from college two years ago.}}
{{agree}}{/əˈɡriː/}{{v. 同意；赞同}}{{I agree with your proposal completely.}}
{{agriculture}}{/ˈæɡrɪkʌltʃər/}{{n. 农业}}{{Agriculture is the backbone of this country's economy.}}
{{ahead}}{/əˈhed/}{{adv. 在前面；提前}}{{The road ahead is clear and smooth.}}
{{aid}}{/eɪd/}{{n. 帮助；援助；v. 援助}}{{The government sent aid to the灾区.}}
{{aim}}{/eɪm/}{{v. 瞄准；旨在；n. 目标}}{{He aims to become a professional musician.}}
{{air}}{/eər/}{{n. 空气；气氛}}{{The air in the mountains is fresh and clean.}}
{{alarm}}{/əˈlɑːrm/}{{n. 警报；惊恐；v. 使惊恐}}{{The fire alarm went off during the meeting.}}
{{album}}{/ˈælbəm/}{{n. 相册；专辑}}{{The band released a new album last month.}}
{{alcohol}}{/ˈælkəhɒl/}{{n. 酒精；酒}}{{Drinking too much alcohol is harmful to health.}}
{{alert}}{/əˈlɜːrt/}{{adj. 警觉的；n. 警报；v. 使警觉}}{{The teacher alerted the students to the danger.}}
{{alien}}{/ˈeɪliən/}{{n. 外星人；adj. 外国的；陌生的}}{{The concept of alien life fascinates many scientists.}}
{{alike}}{/əˈlaɪk/}{{adj. 相似的；adv. 同样地}}{{The two sisters look very much alike.}}
{{alive}}{/əˈlaɪv/}{{adj. 活着的；有活力的}}{{She is the only person alive who knows the truth.}}
{{allow}}{/əˈlaʊ/}{{v. 允许；准许}}{{Smoking is not allowed in this building.}}
